{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Stores","title":"Stores"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","title":"SegmentStore","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L70","fileName":"SegmentStore.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and so is one whose event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What is kept."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Only events of the types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so a type left out of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mistake shows up."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records after it drops some ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading back."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and waits for a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bound.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional one added since is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored at another "},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/versionmismatch(event:storedversion:currentversion:recordcount:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"versionMismatch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"event","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"storedVersion","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"currentVersion","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery read "},{"code":"recordCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" intact records of the event named "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stored at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"storedVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", while the store’s type of that name is at "},{"code":"currentVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and dropped them without decoding them: the version changed for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change their bytes can’t be read through. Reported once per segment, or per database, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each event and stored version, by the event’s name and then the stored version."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","role":"symbol","title":"DropReport.versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)"},"doc://Persistence/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"synchronize"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"synchronize()"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/takeRecoveredRecords()":{"title":"takeRecoveredRecords()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the segments earlier runs left, oldest first, with "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one a delivery had started on; later calls return none."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"takeRecoveredRecords"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/takerecoveredrecords()"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"title":"dropReports","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/writefailed(recordcount:timestamps:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"writeFailed"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timestamps"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SN","text":"ClosedRange"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Writing ","type":"text"},{"code":"recordCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" records, tracked within ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamps","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", to disk failed (the disk is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, say, or segments that couldn’t be deleted fill the bound), so they are kept in memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only: delivered in this run if it lasts long","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enough, lost if it ends first.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"DropReport.writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"title":"RecordStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultDirectory":{"title":"defaultDirectory","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a store keeps its segments unless it is given a directory."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultDirectory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FilePath"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultdirectory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"notPersisted","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"event","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A record of the event named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/undecodable(recordCount:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport.undecodable(recordCount:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"undecodable"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Recovery read ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordCount"},{"text":" intact records it couldn’t decode: their event type isn’t in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":", or its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"text":" threw, as it does for a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before a required property was added or a property’s type changed while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"text":" stayed the same.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/undecodable(recordcount:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A store keeping events of the types ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"directory","type":